(CIP-GEGEVENS KONINKLIJKE BIBLIOTHEEK ?S-GRAVENHAGE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Prologue) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The basic idea of this book is that Keynes?s _General Theory_ is) Tj T*
(generalised even further by including endogenous government in the) Tj T*
(model, so that we arrive at a truly general Political Economy. The) Tj T*
(world had the Great Depression 1930-1940 and has the Great Stagflation) Tj T*
(1970-today and by including ?stagnation in economic policy making? in) Tj T*
(our analysis we find a better explanation. The general theory also) Tj T*
(advises a democracy to create an Economic Supreme Court as a separate) Tj T*
(constitutional power, next to the Legislative, Executive and Judicial) Tj T*
(branches.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This book is primarily directed at my fellow economists and it) Tj T*
(primarily gives theory and stylized facts. The colleagues will) Tj T*
(specifically have to understand the ?Definition & Reality methodology?) Tj T*
(before they will appreciate that my analysis is scientifically) Tj T*
(warranted. Much work remains to be done in practical research. And much) Tj T*
(work remains to be done by the other professions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Since the current imbalance of powers has many victims, it may be) Tj T*
(hoped, none the less, that the parliaments of our democratic nations) Tj T*
(investigate the issue too, so that there is more hope for improvement) Tj T*
(in their living conditions. Parliaments should do as Alfred Marshall) Tj T*
(\(1890, 1947:3\) wrote:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Now at least we are setting ourselves seriously to inquire whether it) Tj T*
(is necessary that there should be any so-called ?lower-classes? at all:) Tj T*
(that is, whether there need be large numbers of people doomed from) Tj T*
(their birth to hard work in order to provide for others the requisites) Tj T*
(of a refined and cultured life; while they themselves are prevented by) Tj T*
(their poverty and toil from having any share or part in that life.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Books are more stimulating and more enjoyable to read if they are) Tj T*
(guided by questions and if they cause questions themselves. This book) Tj T*
(has been written in the style that it provides answers and thus it must) Tj T*
(be feared to be a dull read. It is too late to change that style.) Tj T*
(However, some questions are: \(1\) How is it possible that Europe has an) Tj T*
(unemployment of about 10% for more than three decades now, and the USA) Tj T*
(the mirror image of poverty ? \(2\) Can we really trust our governments ?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
