(1. Order of presentation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The basic idea of this book is that Keynes?s _General Theory_ is) Tj T*
(generalised even further by including endogenous government in the) Tj T*
(model so that we arrive at a truly general Political Economy. The) Tj T*
(argument can be presented in a top-down fashion, for example by) Tj T*
(repeating the IS-LM model before the amendments are introduced. This) Tj T*
(order appears to be uninviting and therefor the argument is presented) Tj T*
(in a bottom-up fashion. We better discuss the amendments before we look) Tj T*
(at the consequences for theory as a whole. We start with the new) Tj T*
(economic synthesis and the argument for the Economic Supreme Court,) Tj T*
(since these motivate the book.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. The general theory) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Political Economy is the science of the management of the state. More) Tj T*
(in general, ?economics? is Greekish for ?management theory?.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([1] Marshall already explained that ?economics? is wider than) Tj T*
(?political economy?, see his ?Principles of economics? \(1947:43\). The) Tj T*
(proper definitions are:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Economics ?in a narrow sense? puts the _approach_, methods and tools,) Tj T*
(of the discipline central, and looks at a variety of subjects.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Political Economy puts the _subject_, the management of the state,) Tj T*
(central.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Economics ?in a broad sense? joins the ?narrow sense? and Political) Tj T*
(Economy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One way to view these distinctions is to visualize a matrix with the) Tj T*
(sciences in the rows and the subjects in the columns. The common) Tj T*
(economist may to some extent neglect the inputs of the other) Tj T*
(disciplines, but the political economist must draw on the resources of) Tj T*
(philosophy, history, law, sociology, politicology, social psychology,) Tj T*
(biology, physics and so on.) Tj T*
([2] Political Economy is, just by definition, the study that tries to) Tj T*
(integrate all human knowledge about the management of the state.) Tj T*
(Political Economy is, in that respect, the proper continuation of) Tj T*
(ancient philosophy on that subject matter.) Tj T*
ET
