(The reasons to adopt these definitions are rather mundane. The King -) Tj T*
(and the ruling elite - can derive their wealth \(a\) from exploitation or) Tj T*
(\(b\) from general productivity growth. The latter is more advantageous) Tj T*
(in the longer run. [4] Productivity can be increased in basically two) Tj T*
(ways: by technology or by management. For example, computers can add to) Tj T*
(our wealth, and we must have technology to be able to have computers.) Tj T*
(But a room full of computers does not present much value if we don?t) Tj T*
(manage their use. So technology and management are the two sides of the) Tj T*
(coin of human wealth. Though no study should neglect either side, there) Tj T*
(of course is advantage in some specialisation of those studies. The) Tj T*
(engineers take one side, the economists the other.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Psychologists and artists might object to that view, and argue that) Tj T*
(proper training in enjoyment and in particular the arts could teach) Tj T*
(people to enjoy life so much more, requiring neither additional) Tj T*
(engineering nor economics. In a sense, this viewpoint would seem to be) Tj T*
(correct. In another sense, it apparently isn?t sufficient. Human beings) Tj T*
(get used to levels of wealth, and require more wealth. It would be) Tj T*
(economics again to study why people are not happy eating bananas and) Tj T*
(watching sunsets. And dealing with issues like this, is management) Tj T*
(again.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Also, when writing this in 2000, and again 2004, there are some rumours) Tj T*
(about the ?end of the state? and the ?loss of power of existing) Tj T*
(nation-states?. This clarifies that the definition of ?Political) Tj T*
(Economy? subsequently requires a definition of the ?state?. I will not) Tj T*
(try to give that here.) Tj T*
([5] For the purposes of this book it suffices to take the existing) Tj T*
(nation-states, and international governmental bodies, and we can) Tj T*
(reconsider that assumption when they all drop their constitutions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Then: The economic process can be understood much better if economic) Tj T*
(policy making itself is included as one of the factors, and then is) Tj T*
(studied from the Public Choice perspective. The basic proposition of) Tj T*
(this book hence is that we can extend the current ?neoclassical) Tj T*
(synthesis? by including endogenous government in the model, so that we) Tj T*
(arrive at a truly general Political Economy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This extension causes the subsequent proposition that it would be) Tj T*
(advisable for a democratic society to create an Economic Supreme Court) Tj T*
(as a separate power in the constitution next to ?Trias Politica? of the) Tj T*
(Legislative, Executive and Judicial branches.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is useful to recall that economics does not restrict its attention) Tj T*
(to ?income? only, but also considers rights and duties. Coase?s theorem) Tj T*
(is a good result in an older tradition. Sen \(1999\)?s ?Development as) Tj T*
(freedom? is a welcome refresher. Beckerman \(1999\) explains that when) Tj T*
(economic growth causes our grandchildren to be wealthier than us) Tj T*
(anyhow, that we should rather focus on bequeathing a good system of) Tj T*
