() Tj T*
(The basic argument is the following. Governments already have economic) Tj T*
(planning bureau?s - the US for example have the Council of Economic) Tj T*
(Advisers to the President. [6] Current forecasts are conditional on the) Tj T*
(assumption that the government will do as planned and promised. Such) Tj T*
(forecasts often fail, and can be forecasted to fail if one takes an) Tj T*
(independent position. Proper forecasting requires that the economic) Tj T*
(adviser not only has a scientific attitude, but also a scientific) Tj T*
(position, and is able to tell and indeed tells the public that plans or) Tj T*
(promises will fail if there is scientific reason for thinking so. Given) Tj T*
(the experience of the 20th century, it appears that strong) Tj T*
(constitutional safeguards are required to provide for this public) Tj T*
(function. Hence an Economic Supreme Court.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Keynes \(1936\) already formulated a ?general theory? for political) Tj T*
(economy. Keynes subsumed the ?classical? approach as a special case.) Tj T*
([7]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Keynes?s theory is rich in many respects and poor in other. On the poor) Tj T*
(side: Keynes?s book is not exact on many issues, and proper models like) Tj T*
(the IS-LM model were only developed by Hicks, Meade and others.) Tj T*
(Samuelson \(1947\) presented the first integration of both the) Tj T*
(competitive model and the utility maximising calculus, only then giving) Tj T*
(body to the notion of ?classical?. [8] However, on the rich side:) Tj T*
(Keynes?s book was and still is a source of inspiration for new research) Tj T*
(angles. Note that Samuelson coined the phrase ?neoclassical synthesis?) Tj T*
(for ?his? conceptual integration of classical processes at the micro) Tj T*
(level and Keynesian processes at the macro level. This synthesis) Tj T*
(endures till today, as e.g. Colignatus \(1990a\), Blanchard \(1999\) and) Tj T*
(Krugman \(1999\) acknowledge. It is important to note, though, that) Tj T*
(Samuelson?s phrase is a bit awkward, since Keynes himself already) Tj T*
(proposed such synthesis - he namely did not abandon micro-economics. It) Tj T*
(would be wrong to associate Keynes only with the macro-economic leg of) Tj T*
(the synthesis. Thus the neoclassical synthesis is actually the) Tj T*
(Keynesian synthesis itself. But we may as well use the phrase) Tj T*
(?neoclassical synthesis?, if only to acknowledge the role of others.) Tj T*
([9]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
