(but also in the standard macro-economic core. A student who considers) Tj T*
(recent textbooks on economics, such as Mankiw \(1992 and 1998\) or) Tj T*
(Dornbusch & Fischer \(1994\), notes that the core of macro-economics) Tj T*
(still derives from Keynes \(1936\) and from the interpretation of his) Tj T*
(theory by the IS-LM model developed by Hicks \(1937\) and others. The) Tj T*
(ongoing discussion since 1936 can only be understood by properly) Tj T*
(including these original theoretical roots. Krugman gives a useful) Tj T*
(refresher in his ?The return of depression economics? \(1999\). Flanning) Tj T*
(& Mahony \(1998, 2000\) provide a recommendable modern summary companion) Tj T*
(to _The General Theory_ that is a testimony of its relevance. The) Tj T*
