(3. Methodology) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Methodology appears to be important in this book. Sometimes, paradigm) Tj T*
(shifts are as much a matter of methodology as a matter of content.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One example is Keynes. As an economist, Keynes emphasised the economic) Tj T*
(content of his analysis: notably his findings on the peculiar role of) Tj T*
(money in the economy. His observation is firstly that money is both a) Tj T*
(medium of exchange and a store of value, and secondly that storage) Tj T*
(value depends upon expected value: and then his analysis on) Tj T*
(expectations takes off. In retrospect the force of Keynes?s analysis is) Tj T*
(a bit less ?economics? than he thought, and has more to do with the) Tj T*
(handling of time than with money per se. Samuelson \(1947, 1983:117\) and) Tj T*
(Grandmont \(1983\) showed that the analysis can be reproduced if money is) Tj T*
(entered in the utility functions. What remains is the issue of time.) Tj T*
