(wages \(which would increase unemployment\), the only solution seems to) Tj T*
(be the reduction of benefits. This was actually the statement of the) Tj T*
(Dutch Minister of Social Affairs at the presentation of the Dutch) Tj T*
(National Budget in September 1999. Even the small Socialist Party \(SP\)) Tj T*
(accepts this view, vide its January 2000 internet site. The Minister) Tj T*
(and the oppostion party however are misguided and badly advised. In the) Tj T*
(proper analysis the problem is crucially different. If there would be) Tj T*
(sufficient jobs then there already are regulations that people can be) Tj T*
(fined for not accepting a job offer. This fine creates an incentive of) Tj T*
(30% in a warning stage and eventually 100% by full withdrawal of the) Tj T*
(benefit. So the problem is rather that there are insufficient job) Tj T*
(offers - with sounds more like a demand problem. By manipulating taxes,) Tj T*
(it is possible to reduce gross wage costs - and increase demand - while) Tj T*
(still allowing for a decent net income.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Another point of attention is the word ?unemployment?. Holland in 1999) Tj T*
(features an ?official unemployment rate? of about 3.2 %. It seems as if) Tj T*
(unemployment is no problem for Holland. As an economist I however) Tj T*
(cannot accept the sausage that the Statistical Office \(in this case the) Tj T*
(Dutch CPB and CBS\) here present. \(1\) Dutch ?official disability? is) Tj T*
(about 10% of the true labour force, \(2\) people older than 55 years are) Tj T*
(often excluded from the ?official labour force? too, \(3\) many people) Tj T*
(work part-time since they cannot find a full-time job, \(4\) many women) Tj T*
(will not work outdoors since childcare is too expensive because of the) Tj T*
(wrong wages, \(5\) etcetera. Many economists classify these issues under) Tj T*
(the denominator of ?participation?, and then agree that Holland has a) Tj T*
(participation problem. However, in proper economic terms it is) Tj T*
(unemployment: people who would want jobs but cannot find them. I urge) Tj T*
(the statisticians to remain servient to economic science, as they claim) Tj T*
(they are, rather than servient to politics and disinformation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
