(A note on the negative income tax) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A common topic in the subject of taxation is the concept of a negative) Tj T*
(income tax \(NIT\). A person below a certain threshold receives money) Tj T*
(instead of paying it. The negative income tax can be presented as a) Tj T*
(?basic benefit?: all members of society receive allowance _A _from the) Tj T*
(state, and pay taxes only on their additional income. The negative) Tj T*
(income tax or basic benefit is often presented as a solution to the) Tj T*
(current unemployment problem. The Central Planning Bureau \(1992a&b\) in) Tj T*
(fact shows that this can work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is useful to clarify the following. We can distinguish three groups) Tj T*
(with different effects:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· for the currently employed the NIT has no effect, since they already) Tj T*
(are employed and in fact already earn their own basic benefit) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· for the people in the Tax Void, the NIT effectively only means the) Tj T*
(increase of exemption, and thus one might as well increase exemption) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· for workers with sub-subsistence productivity, the NIT indeed) Tj T*
(provides additional revenue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The second effect cannot properly be regarded as a positive effect of a) Tj T*
(NIT. Only the last effect is the NIT proper. However, proponents of the) Tj T*
(NIT often include the second group when they claim good results. In the) Tj T*
(current situation of mass unemployment, the employment effect will also) Tj T*
(be largest for the second group, so the effects of the NIT are grossly) Tj T*
(overstated. You may be familiar with the joke of the mouse and the) Tj T*
(elephant walking on a bridge, and the mouse proclaiming: ?We make quite) Tj T*
(a lot of noise together, don?t we ??) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It must be noted that proposals on the NIT generally state huge sums of) Tj T*
(money. The NIT is very ?expensive? since all spouses would apply,) Tj T*
(causing the need for more changes in the tax code. [97]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The NIT complexities, and huge sums, also obscure the fact that) Tj T*
(abolishing the Tax Void would be for free. Proponents of the NIT thus) Tj T*
(can be compared to people at Amsterdam Schiphol airport wanting to go) Tj T*
(to Washington, and waiting at the ticket booth till they have enough) Tj T*
(money to buy the expensive ticket, while they overlook that, due to) Tj T*
(circumstances, the plane to New York flies for free.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The concept of a NIT, intended to do good, generally seems to cause) Tj T*
(people to do a lot of harm. The Central Planning Bureau \(1992a&b\) study) Tj T*
(assumed the gradual introduction of a NIT in the course of 25 years,) Tj T*
(keeping subsistence fixed at a constant inflation adjusted value of) Tj T*
(1990, and the NIT fully introduced at that value in 2015. This scenario) Tj T*
(thus has the drawbacks of \(a\) achieving full employment only in 2015,) Tj T*
(\(b\) not indexing subsistence to general welfare.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It may well be that the Ministry of Finance is less equipped to deal) Tj T*
