(external imbalance. But we can reproduce the difference in reactions of) Tj T*
(the two sectors. We may study situations_ with _full employment) Tj T*
(\(1950-1970\) and _without _this \(1970-2005\). Below, we give a model,) Tj T*
(tables and graphs.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Model) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Regard a general equilibrium model with 15 units of highly productive) Tj T*
(labour \(_h_\), 75 units of modally productive labour \(_m_\) and 10 units) Tj T*
(of lowly productive, minimum wage workers and possible benefit) Tj T*
(recipients \(_l_\). The economy has exposed and sheltered sectors that) Tj T*
(produce output _yE   _and _yS_, while a social welfare function \(SWF\)) Tj T*
(determines the optimal combination. In an open model, the _yE_ would be) Tj T*
