(Investment, growth and productivity) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The following has been in my mind since Colignatus \(1989\) but was not) Tj T*
(stated in the first edition of this book. One of the key points of) Tj T*
(Keynes in the _General Theory_ was that the true, real, savings of an) Tj T*
(economy consist of what is invested. All the money that people save) Tj T*
(does not count as an investment or real saving. Whatever amount they) Tj T*
(bring to the banks or even hide under their beds, it is only money. One) Tj T*
(can have nominal saving _S _and price level _P, _but the division _S /) Tj T*
(P _is more psychological than real._ _What counts are the houses built,) Tj T*
(bridges constructed, lessons learnt, all that can be carried over to) Tj T*
(the next period. In fact, a company that produces but can?t sell and) Tj T*
(goes bankrupt might actually do society a favour, since at least some) Tj T*
(goods have been produced which otherwise might not have come into) Tj T*
(existence. The challenge is to get production and investment without) Tj T*
(such perceived incompetence or fraud. The economy should be designed so) Tj T*
(that those investments come about in an optimal way, where the optimum) Tj T*
(must be defined not only in terms of expectations and stability but) Tj T*
(also in terms of social welfare and full employment.) Tj T*
