(33. Introduction) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Kenneth Arrow \(1950, 1951, 1963\) presented an Impossibility Theorem in) Tj T*
(which he showed that decisions about ?the general welfare? are) Tj T*
(impossible in certain cases or have to be left to a dictator. Arrow) Tj T*
(presented some five axioms that each seemed reasonable when considered) Tj T*
(by itself, and he argued as well that these axioms are morally) Tj T*
(desirable and fitting to the concept of ?general welfare?. He also) Tj T*
(formulated the problem in general terms so that it concerns choices on) Tj T*
(goods or people. Subsequently, he derived a contradiction. This result) Tj T*
(caused quite some consternation, but eventually the mathematical rigour) Tj T*
(caused acceptance, and since then the Theorem forms the core of many) Tj T*
(books, such as Sen \(1970\) and Mueller\(1989\). The Theorem was also one) Tj T*
(of the reasons to award Arrow the Nobel Prize in economics.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A voting example is given by the US Presidential election of 2000.) Tj T*
(Apart from the problems around the ballot process itself, there was a) Tj T*
(more basic problem: with main contenders Bush, Gore and Nader, Bush got) Tj T*
(elected, but in another system, such as a run-off between the two) Tj T*
(?major? contenders, the Nader vote apparently would have switched) Tj T*
(largely to Gore, making him the US President. So the choice depends as) Tj T*
(much upon the system chosen as on the preferences. Can we find a) Tj T*
(generally good system ? Arrow?s Theorem suggests ?No?.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Arrow?s Theorem has had a huge influence on scientific and political) Tj T*
(thought. Part of this influence is subtle, where skepsis arises about) Tj T*
(the concept of ?democracy?. That shiny goal loses its appeal when we) Tj T*
(don?t know how representatives should be elected and when morally) Tj T*
(desirable rules would be impossible. Opting for the natural forces in) Tj T*
(the social process may be more pragmatic. The influence of the Theorem) Tj T*
(can sometimes be more explicit. Next to the model of the utility) Tj T*
(maximising individual, there is the model for society as a whole and) Tj T*
(then the maximisation of a Social Welfare Function \(SWF\). But when a) Tj T*
(morally acceptable SWF is impossible, what would be the use of research) Tj T*
(into such an inherently flawed concept ? Many nations co-ordinate their) Tj T*
(economic policy, and have created institutions for this, like the) Tj T*
(Council of Economic Advisors \(US\), the Commissariat du Plan \(France\),) Tj T*
(the Sachverständigenrat \(Germany\), and the Central Planning Bureau) Tj T*
(\(Holland\). Such an institution, given its role in the co-ordination of) Tj T*
(economic policy, could be expected to do reseach on the national SWF.) Tj T*
(However, those institutions tend to abstain from that kind of research,) Tj T*
(pointing to Arrow?s Theorem as one of the arguments, if not the major) Tj T*
ET
endstream
