(results into _B < C _which differs from _B = C_. Contradiction. Thus) Tj T*
(there is a counterexample to the axioms. So the axioms are) Tj T*
(inconsistent. Q.E.D.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The merit of this short proof is that it clearly shows the awkwardness) Tj T*
(of the _APDM._ In the case of Condorcet?s example the conclusion _B =) Tj T*
(C_ is a sound decision, and in the case of the adjusted example the) Tj T*
(conclusion _B < C_ is sound too. That preferences outside of the pair) Tj T*
(_B _and _C _ have changed is_ vital_ to the group decision, since the) Tj T*
(shift helps a change from clear indifference to clear preference. The) Tj T*
(preferences on other topics are quite relevant, and not ?irrelevant?.) Tj T*
(_APDM _excludes vital information about the preferences - to be) Tj T*
(precise: it destroys information that exists - and it should come as no) Tj T*
(surprise that paradoxes and inconsistencies arise. The _APDM _is) Tj T*
(incongruent with the notion of group decision making. Perhaps an) Tj T*
(individual can exclude information about other topics, but a group) Tj T*
(cannot. \(Or a brain that works as a group cannot.\) It is a surprise) Tj T*
(that _APDM _has not been killed right in 1951.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A note on the name of APDM) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Arrow \(1951, 1963\) introduced an axiom ?Independence of Irrelevant) Tj T*
