(There are two key conclusions:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(1\)    The Pareto condition for the candidates under ballot should not) Tj T*
(be neglected - i.e. that only those candidates are voted on that are an) Tj T*
(improvement compared to the _status quo_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(2\)    The Borda Fixed Point can be seen as a compromise between the) Tj T*
(Borda and Condorcet procedures \(on Paretian points\), and provides a) Tj T*
(degree of protection against budget changes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is also another conclusion. Voting is complex, and becomes) Tj T*
(increasingly complex when the numbers of candidates and voters rise) Tj T*
(\(especially when we also include indifference and not just strict) Tj T*
(preference\). Direct election of a President becomes quickly infeasible) Tj T*
(for the more advanced voting procedures. From this observation we can) Tj T*
(conclude that it is better to have a proportional parlementary system,) Tj T*
(so that the elected professionals can use the advanced voting) Tj T*
(procedures to select the President. This approach of representation) Tj T*
(also prevents that there is a different electoral mandate for President) Tj T*
(versus Parliament. Note that the discussion above, on Arrow?s Theorem) Tj T*
(and the Borda Fixed Point method, considers single seat elections, and) Tj T*
(not multi-seat elections. But the complexity of direct single seat) Tj T*
(elections tends to support this conclusion on the overall system of) Tj T*
(proportional representation and indirect election of the chief) Tj T*
(executives.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(36. Some notes on ethics) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The following notes on ethics are not well developed but the points are) Tj T*
(useful to observe.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(a\)    I was struck by Keynes?s quote: ?along the line of origin at) Tj T*
(least, economics - more properly called political economy - is a side) Tj T*
(of ethics? \(Skidelsky \(2000:264\)\). This is a point that is commonly not) Tj T*
(seen by the general public who associate economics with money, and) Tj T*
(neither by many economists who don?t appreciate the subject of) Tj T*
(political economy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(b\)    Ethics focusses on survival and the good life \(?flourishing?\).) Tj T*
(That is, just like laboratory animals require an optimal environment,) Tj T*
(humans have their own conditions for flourishing. Csikszentmihalyi) Tj T*
(\(1997\), ?Living well. The psychology of everyday life?, clarifies the) Tj T*
(required balance between challenge and competence: too much challenge) Tj T*
(causes stress while too little challenge causes boredom. The Rasch) Tj T*
(model, also known in psychology as the item-response model, or the Elo) Tj T*
(model used for Elo rating in chess, seems to fit the situation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
