() Tj T*
(Introduction) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This May 1 2004, the European Union enlarges with the new member states) Tj T*
(of Central Europe. This is a joyous occasion to celebrate and it is) Tj T*
(also an occasion to look back at the past and ahead to the future to) Tj T*
(see what lessons can be learned.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One of the important issues to consider is unemployment. Unemployment) Tj T*
(is a horrible economic disease since it threatens the very existence of) Tj T*
(the unemployed person and his or her family, and it increases the) Tj T*
(stress in society as a whole. France and Germany still have) Tj T*
(unemployment levels of almost 10% of the working force, the new member) Tj T*
(states wish they were so lucky. It is not obvious that the Enlargement) Tj T*
(will generate the creative energy to resolve the problem, and some) Tj T*
(people fear that there will only be additional problems. Hence at the) Tj T*
(occasion of the Enlargement it is proper to try to determine what can) Tj T*
(be done.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In 1989-1990, I wrote Colignatus \(1990a\), ?After 20 years of mass) Tj T*
(unemployment: Why we might wish for a parliamentary inquiry? as an) Tj T*
(internal note of the Dutch Central Planning Bureau \(CPB\). The abstract) Tj T*
(and summary are reproduced in the appendix to this chapter below while) Tj T*
(the full text can be found at my website. We are now 15 years further) Tj T*
(and this explains the first part of the title of this paper: ?After 35) Tj T*
(years of mass unemployment?.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(What remains to discuss is how we move from a wish for a parliamentary) Tj T*
(enquiry to an advice to boycott Holland. The point is that the 1990) Tj T*
(paper contains the solution for unemployment but met with censorship by) Tj T*
(the CPB directorate, and Dutch society has not been able to resolve) Tj T*
(that censorship yet. I have grown convinced that an outside influence) Tj T*
(will be of use and that in fact only a boycott of Holland can help out.) Tj T*
(Hence, my advice to the rest of the world is to boycott Holland till) Tj T*
(the Dutch resolve the censorship of science by the directorate of the) Tj T*
(Dutch Central Planning Bureau. The remainder of this paper is devoted) Tj T*
(to development of that argument.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(First considerations) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is useful to explain the following about the Dutch Central Planning) Tj T*
(Bureau. The CPB has a similar role in Holland as the Council of) Tj T*
(Economic Advisers to the President in the USA in the co-ordination of) Tj T*
(economic policy making. The CPB is a world renowned institute. When it) Tj T*
(was founded shortly after World War II, the first director was Jan) Tj T*
(Tinbergen who later received the Nobel Prize for his pioneering work in) Tj T*
(econometrics. Other economists at CPB of historical fame are for) Tj T*
(example Theil, Koyck, Verdoorn, De Wolff \(who is less known but for) Tj T*
(example coined the terms ?macro-economics? and ?micro-economics?\). The) Tj T*
(CPB director who originally censored my analysis and who fired me with) Tj T*
(an abuse of science is Gerrit Zalm, now better known in European) Tj T*
(politics as the Dutch Minister of Finance. The current CPB director is) Tj T*
ET
endstream
