(no.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A key example is The Economic Journal, Volume 114, no 494, March 2004.) Tj T*
(There is the presidential address by professor Stephen Nickell of the) Tj T*
(Bank of England and the London School of Economics, and there is a) Tj T*
(special session on the UK minimum wage, with five papers by renowned) Tj T*
(authors. All these authors have my highest respect and their work is) Tj T*
(crucial for understanding the economic situation. But solution to) Tj T*
(unemployment isn?t there yet, while it is available for discussion.) Tj T*
(I fully agree with professor Nickell and I thank him for his) Tj T*
(observation:) Tj T*
(?Relative poverty in the UK has risen massively since 1979 mainly) Tj T*
(because of increasing worklessnes, rising earnings dispersion and) Tj T*
(benefits indexed to prices, not wages. So poverty is now at a very high) Tj T*
(level.?) Tj T*
(Professor Nickell suggests ?reducing the long tail in the skill) Tj T*
(distribution?, but in my analysis we should also consider the tax void) Tj T*
(and the dynamic marginal tax rates, so that more low-skilled people can) Tj T*
(start working \(also because of ?learning by doing?\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Since all these other ways have had little effect, I can usefully) Tj T*
(advise to boycott Holland to speed up matters.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The line of reasoning thus is that if you want to resolve mass) Tj T*
(unemployment then you need the theory that is blocked from internal) Tj T*
(discussion by the directorate of the Dutch CPB. Since other ways fail,) Tj T*
(a boycott of Holland can be a good way to resolve the issue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This is an advice and not an appeal. I am not an activist, but a) Tj T*
(scientist. It is only sound advice for the citizen who wants mass) Tj T*
