(\(May 1, 2004\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Appendix: After 20 years of mass unemployment:) Tj T*
(Why we might wish for a parliamentary inquiry) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(Abstract and summary only\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(http://www.dataweb.nl/~cool/Thomas/Nederlands/TPnCPB/Record/1990/12/18/) Tj T*
(index.html) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thomas Colignatus  *  December 18 1990) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CPB internal note 90-III-38) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Abstract) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A synthesis of economic theory is presented, the solution to) Tj T*
(unemployment is restated, the intellectual need for a parliamentary) Tj T*
(inquiry is established, and as an example to such inquiry the) Tj T*
(performance of the _Centraal Planbureau _is evaluated.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Summary) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In Holland, mass unemployment persists already for about twenty years,) Tj T*
(and will continue to do so for many years to come.  Economists agree on) Tj T*
(the obvious solution, the reduction of labour costs. But for some) Tj T*
(reasons our decision making process doesn?t generate that decision.) Tj T*
(Policy measures that are taken, actually are troublesome, like the) Tj T*
(creation of a _Centraal Bureau voor de Arbeidsvoorziening _\(CBA\), or) Tj T*
(the recent ?temporary and red tape? ten percent subsidy on minimum) Tj T*
(wages \(WLOM\). The policymaking situation is analyzed in a more formal) Tj T*
(manner, to allow for more abstract reasoning. This requires a social) Tj T*
(welfare function, an income redistribution function, and a production) Tj T*
(function \(for the unemployed cq. subsidized workers\). In fact, we might) Tj T*
(attain the goals of high growth, price stability, full employment and a) Tj T*
(just income distribution, by means of monetary, fiscal and subsidy) Tj T*
(instruments. The conclusion however is that the present policy) Tj T*
(sclerosis derives from insufficient interest in and information about) Tj T*
(the form and location of those mentioned functions, and lack of) Tj T*
(interest In optimization itself; and_ _this again may be caused by) Tj T*
(institutional weak spots. A review of the issue and of the policymaking) Tj T*
(process could be beneficial and actually logically needed. Among) Tj T*
(others, this would include a review of the _Centraal Planbureau _\(CPB\),) Tj T*
(that has not properly endogenised government behaviour in its models,) Tj T*
(projections and analyses. It is suggested that such review would be a) Tj T*
(task for parliament; and the logic for a so-called _parlementaire) Tj T*
(enquete _is compelling. Clarity on the issues is essential too for the) Tj T*
(European debate and our advice to the Eastern European countries.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(*\) The author is an econometrician at a government agency that has some) Tj T*
(involvement with the economic policy making process; the article) Tj T*
(expresses his own views only. This paper is adapted from a presentation) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
