() Tj T*
(Appendices) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On the definition of economics) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The body of the text explains the difference of and relationship) Tj T*
(between ?economics? and ?political economy?. I propose that we all) Tj T*
(stick to those definitions. But it remains useful to relate to) Tj T*
(definitions provided by other authors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Marshall \(1890, 1947, p1 and 43\) first equates Political Economy and) Tj T*
(Economics, and then splits them up again:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Political Economy or Economics is a study of mankind in the ordinary) Tj T*
(business of life; it examines that part of individual and social action) Tj T*
(which is most closely connected with the attainment and with the use of) Tj T*
(the material requisites of wellbeing.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Economics is thus taken to mean a study of the economic aspects and) Tj T*
(conditions of man?s political, social and private life; but more) Tj T*
(especially of his social life. The aims of the study are to gain) Tj T*
(knowledge for its own sake, and to obtain guidance in the practical) Tj T*
(conduct of life, and especially of social life. The need for such) Tj T*
(guidance was never so urgent as now; a later generation may have more) Tj T*
(abundant leisure than we for researches that throw light on obscure) Tj T*
(points in abstract speculation, or in the history of past times, but do) Tj T*
(not afford immediate aid in present difficulties.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(But though thus largely directed by practical needs, economics avoids) Tj T*
(as far as possible the discussion of those exigencies of party) Tj T*
ET
