(organization, and those diplomacies of home and foreign politics of) Tj T*
(which the statesman is bound to take account in deciding what measures) Tj T*
(that he can propose will bring him nearest to the end that he desires) Tj T*
(to secure for his country. It aims indeed at helping him to determine) Tj T*
(not only what that end should be, but also what are the best methods of) Tj T*
(a broad policy devoted to that end. But it shuns many political issues,) Tj T*
(which the practical man cannot ignore: and it is therefore a science,) Tj T*
(pure and applied, rather than a science and an art. And it is better) Tj T*
(described by the broad term ?Economics? than by the narrower term) Tj T*
(?Political Economy?.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Here, ?economic aspects and conditions? refer to the provision for food) Tj T*
(and shelter, the working life etcetera. Nowadays we would tend to) Tj T*
(include more subjects, and still say that ?economics? is involved in) Tj T*
(it. To us, ?economics? sets in \(as a sufficient but not necessary) Tj T*
(condition\) as soon when some preference decision is to be made.) Tj T*
(Marshall?s tools, as for example the scissors of supply and demand,) Tj T*
(have been applied to this wider area of application too. This indeed) Tj T*
(may well be the luxury situation that he expected.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(By consequence, it is useful to still use the name ?economics? for the) Tj T*
(wider subject areas, even though allowing for more subjects causes less) Tj T*
(?economic content? than Marshall perceived. Economics thus is) Tj T*
(characterised by the approach, method and tools used. On the other) Tj T*
(hand, ?political economy? then concentrates on one particular subject:) Tj T*
(the management of the state. Much of Marshall?s ?Principles? will,) Tj T*
(paradoxically, then be relevant for political economy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Gambs and Komisar?s 1968 textbook  ?Economics and man?, chapter 1,) Tj T*
(gives a nice overview of the various definitions that early economists) Tj T*
(have provided. A longer quote \(of those quotes\) usefully enriches our) Tj T*
(understanding of the definition of ?political economy?.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?What is economics all about? It is often defined as the science of) Tj T*
(wealth or as the study of how mankind gets its living. Statements like) Tj T*
(this are certainly useful, but they are also too general. When we try) Tj T*
(to take the next step, we get into trouble. We meet difficulties in) Tj T*
(pinning economics down because its practitioners are in disagreement) Tj T*
(about the scope and nature of their science, and at­tempts to) Tj T*
(particularize lead to protests from opposing schools of thought. The) Tj T*
(only definitions on which agreement is possible are broad ones like) Tj T*
(those given above, or humorous ones like ?Economics is whatever an) Tj T*
(economist wants to talk about.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The reader may have misgivings about studying a science in which) Tj T*
(disagreements arise at the very start. His doubts are indeed well) Tj T*
(founded but should not too quickly turn him away. After all, there are) Tj T*
(still differences of opinion even in astronomy and phyics, chemistry) Tj T*
(and biology. Psychology remains a free-for-all. No considerable field) Tj T*
(of knowledge is so completely understood that all of its scholars speak) Tj T*
(with the same voice. The process of reaching a balanced conclu­sion) Tj T*
(often requires a sifting of the testimony of contradictory witnesses.) Tj T*
