() Tj T*
(Economics is a study of the ?community?s methods of turning material) Tj T*
(things to account? \(Thorstein Veblen, 1857?1929\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Economics ... is concerned with that aspect of behavior which arises) Tj T*
(from the scarcity of means to achieve given ends \(Lionel Robbins, 1898?) Tj T*
(\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(. . . Economics is ... a social science; that is, it deals with the) Tj T*
(behavior of men in organized communities. Its special province is the) Tj T*
(behavior of social groups in providing the means for attaining their) Tj T*
(various ends \(Wesley Mitchell, 1874?1948\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The theory of economics ? is a method rather than a doctrine, an) Tj T*
(apparatus of the mind, a technique of thinking, which helps its) Tj T*
(possessor to draw correct conclusions \(John Maynard Keynes, 1883?1946\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A few comments on the above may help. The first definition, by Steuart) Tj T*
(was conceived before much formal and sustained thought by a succession) Tj T*
(of scholars had been given to what we now name ?economics?. Steuart was) Tj T*
(a mercantilist, primarily interesed in the wealth of the British crown) Tj T*
(and its capacity to support a navy, pay soldiers, and build and) Tj T*
(maintain the King?s highways. His concern was not with the nation as a) Tj T*
(whole ? the artisans, farmers, and other men of low degree. In) Tj T*
(contrast, the next definition, by Mill ?  a very acceptable definition) Tj T*
(even today ? does consider the society as a whole. It also calls) Tj T*
(attention to the ?laws of ... production and distribution.? which are) Tj T*
(still at the forefront of economic interest. With the exception of the) Tj T*
(definition given by Lionel Robbins, all of the others reach down ? like) Tj T*
(Mill ? into the entire community. Veblen and Mitchell are dissenting) Tj T*
(economists \(?\) Yet both echo the phrase of Marshall, a major orthodox) Tj T*
(econ­omist, about ?the attainment . . . of the material requisites of) Tj T*
(well being.? Marshall, Robbins, and Mitchell place emphasis on human) Tj T*
(behavior. This is a desirable emphasis, lest we forget because of our) Tj T*
(shorthand way of speaking that human beings are the cause of economic) Tj T*
(phenomena. For example, economists are much concerned about the rise) Tj T*
(and fall of prices; but prices do not rise and fall. Human beings mark) Tj T*
(them up or down. The majority of American standard or orthodox) Tj T*
(economists would endorse the definition given by Marshall, not only) Tj T*
(because it is a good one, but also because of his great authority. Yet) Tj T*
(Robbins? ? so completely different?would also meet with great favor.) Tj T*
(What economists like about this pithy definition is that it goes to the) Tj T*
(heart of an issue which engrosses many of them: how to reconcile) Tj T*
(scarcity or the niggardliness of nature with the unlimited desires of) Tj T*
(man. Economists like to say they will not be needed in heaven. The) Tj T*
(reason is that in paradise, wants are few and resources boundless. Its) Tj T*
(inhabitants will never have to decide how much to spend and how much to) Tj T*
(save, how heavily to tax, how much butter to give up in order to have) Tj T*
(guns.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The definition given by Keynes, the most widely acclaimed economist of) Tj T*
(the 20th century, is a rather puzzling one. Economics is here defined) Tj T*
