(partly as a ?technique of thinking.? What does this mean? Obviously,) Tj T*
(any organized body of knowledge directs the mind in ways that are) Tj T*
(foreign to other organized bodies of knowledge. The chemist thinks) Tj T*
(about how atoms combine, whether they combine explosively or quietly,) Tj T*
(what happens when you restructure the atoms of a molecule. In this) Tj T*
(sense, we get a unique ?technique of thinking? in almost any) Tj T*
(specialized activity, including economics; indeed, even baseball,) Tj T*
(football, and other sports impose a special technique of thinking, But) Tj T*
(is his all that Keynes has in mind? Certain well-known techniques of) Tj T*
(thinking include induction and deduction. Behaviorist psychologists ?) Tj T*
(at least in the early days?reduced thinking to in­audible speech; the) Tj T*
(philosopher John Dewey described thinking as problem solving. Without) Tj T*
(clarifying, Keynes seems to claim for economics a unique method of) Tj T*
(ascertaining truth?one which is either a substitute for or an addition) Tj T*
(to the more widely known methods suggested above; something you would) Tj T*
(not find in a book of logic, only in a book of economics. If this is) Tj T*
(his meaning, we must reject the definition, for the method of) Tj T*
(scientific investigation and techniques of thought are the same for all) Tj T*
(kinds of data; and in any case, there is a difference between the) Tj T*
(concerns and data of economics and the method of studying it ? a) Tj T*
(difference which is not recognized in the Keynesian definition.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The question whether economics is really a science cannot be answered) Tj T*
(easily. Astronomy, chemistry and physics have spoiled us with their) Tj T*
(split-second accuracy and such infallibility of prediction that we are) Tj T*
(inclined to look with disdain at the social sciences. Biology has not) Tj T*
(scored the successes credited to the physical sciences, but it still) Tj T*
(outpaces economics by a good deal. If, however, science is thought of) Tj T*
(as an attitude, a willingness to put aside prejudice, self-interest,) Tj T*
(and the unverified wisdom of the authority, then economics will fare) Tj T*
(moderately well.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This ends the longer quote.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Gambs and Komisar themselves state: ?The economist?s job in our society) Tj T*
(- as it would be in simpler societies - is to study all of our) Tj T*
(decision-making forces, practices, and traditions, and to decide) Tj T*
(whether they are promoting the general welfare.? \(p14\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(My own notes on all of this: \(1\) Keynes?s quote likely refers to the) Tj T*
(?science? claim for economics, and has less to do with its subject) Tj T*
(matter. See the discussion on Hicks in chapter 19. \(2\) Robbins?s) Tj T*
(definition, though popular as it is - since it focusses on a clear) Tj T*
(phenomenon that can be frequently seen - thus is inadequate on the) Tj T*
(whole. It is an engineering?s definition, a rephrasing of ?efficiency?.) Tj T*
(It is useful to highlight some aspects, but no more. It neglects policy) Tj T*
(stagnation that causes a state of inefficiency to endure. It neglects) Tj T*
(evolution and power that for example affect the income distribution.) Tj T*
(Robbins?s definition is like defining a map as ?a piece of paper that) Tj T*
(contains street names?, forgetting all the other useful things that map) Tj T*
(makers provide.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
