576 0 obj
<< /Length 3482 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(Mankiw \(1998:4\) defines: ?Economics is the study of how society manages) Tj T*
(its scarce resources.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This again mixes ?economics? \(the approach\) and ?political economy? \(a) Tj T*
(subject\). I am not in favor of this, see the introductory discussion.) Tj T*
(The ?10 principles? that Mankiw himself provides in his first chapter) Tj T*
(give a nice view on the economic approach to problems - quite like) Tj T*
(Keynes?s definition - but do not tell us much yet about the management) Tj T*
(of the state.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Piet de Wolff \(1911-2000\) introduced the distinction ?macro-economics?) Tj T*
(and ?micro-economics?, in his 1941 article on elasticities, in The) Tj T*
(Economic Journal. His distinction is plain technical, and his) Tj T*
(?macro-economics? appears to be just another word for ?aggregate?. I) Tj T*
(surmise that the economics profession quickly adopted the word) Tj T*
(?macro-economics? since it sounds more professional and less political) Tj T*
(than ?Political Economy?. It sounds as a distinction that can be made) Tj T*
(within economics, without having to visit the other sciences. The) Tj T*
(problem with equating macro-economics with Political Economy however is) Tj T*
(that Political Economy also is interested in distributional aspects -) Tj T*
(while macro-economics by definition looks at the aggregate only. A) Tj T*
(problem with publishing a book on micro-economics \(and using that word) Tj T*
(as the title\) is that good micro-economics of course also includes the) Tj T*
(macro-economic feedbacks and constraints. So my suggestion is to use) Tj T*
(the ?macro? and ?micro? words as technical terms only \(better sounding) Tj T*
(than ?aggregate? and ?disaggregate?\), and not write books with those) Tj T*
(titles or create professorial chairs on those ?subjects?.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Biographical note on Montesquieu) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Quoting from) Tj T*
(http://www.geocities.com/Athens/Acropolis/6681/montesqb.htm:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?Montesquieu, Charles Louis de Secondat, Baron de la Brede et de) Tj T*
(\(1689-1755\), French writer and jurist, born in the Chteau of la Brède,) Tj T*
(and educated at the Oratorian school at Juilly and later at Bordeaux.) Tj T*
(He became counselor of the Bordeaux parliament in 1714 and was its) Tj T*
(president from 1716 to 1728. Montesquieu first became prominent as a) Tj T*
(writer with his Persian Letters \(1721; trans. 1961\); in this work,) Tj T*
(through the device of letters written to and by two aristocratic) Tj T*
(Persian travelers in Europe, Montesquieu satirized contemporary French) Tj T*
(politics, social conditions, ecclesiastical matters, and literature.) Tj T*
(the book won immediate and wide popularity; it was one of the earliest) Tj T*
(works of the movement known as the Enlightenment, which, by its) Tj T*
(criticism of French institutions under the Bourbon monarchy, helped) Tj T*
(bring about the French Revolution. The reputation acquired by) Tj T*
(Montesquieu through this work and several others of lesser importance) Tj T*
(led to his election to the French Academy in 1728. His second) Tj T*
(significant work was Considérations sur les causes de la grandeur et de) Tj T*
(la décadence des Romains \(Thoughts on the Causes of the Greatness and) Tj T*
(the Downfall of the Romans, 1734\), one of the first important works in) Tj T*
(the philosophy of history. His masterpiece was The Spirit of Laws) Tj T*
ET
endstream
