(after great misgivings. As a rule, a student of economics should always) Tj T*
(read up on the Nobel laureates, but Hayek never inspired me. What I) Tj T*
(read about his work made it uninviting. In Skidelsky?s biography of) Tj T*
(Keynes he is reduced from a critic of Keynes to someone whom Keynes,) Tj T*
(exasparated from lack of progress in communication, took along to go) Tj T*
(and buy old books. Later Hayek got a following of ?libertarians? and) Tj T*
(that was equally unattractive \(not to be confused with ?librarians?) Tj T*
(\(;-\)\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I likely agree with Mark Blaug \(1985:90\): ?In short, everyone agrees) Tj T*
(with what Hayek means in general but there is a large spectrum of) Tj T*
(answers to what he means in particular. It will take another generation) Tj T*
(to fully digest Hayek?s many and multifaceted contributions to) Tj T*
(economics and indeed social science as a whole.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(What I finally got to read of Hayek actually made me better appreciate) Tj T*
(part of his work, though the feelings remain mixed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For starters, it appears that Hayek considers himself to be a ?whig?) Tj T*
(like Gladstone and de Tocqueville, and that he was not too happy with) Tj T*
(the ?libertarians?. This is quite a relief to read, and I am sorry that) Tj T*
(I have entertained such a prejudice for so long. \(And: Why can?t) Tj T*
(reporters be more accurate ?\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Secondly, Hayek is known in current economics for his early comments on) Tj T*
(the relevance of ?knowledge?. My hesitation on this remains, though.) Tj T*
(This hesitation derives from the consideration that he apparently) Tj T*
(didn?t advance beyond Walras?s solution of assuming tatonnement, and) Tj T*
(similarly I find it hard to believe that other early economists) Tj T*
(disregarded knowledge. \(Keynes for example emphasised ?expectations?.\)) Tj T*
(But ?knowlegde? is an issue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Subsequently, though, I was jolted by Hayek?s discussion of the) Tj T*
(philosophical consequences of his theory of knowledge. Some of his) Tj T*
(thoughts are precisely the same as mine ! Notably \(I could not have) Tj T*
(said it better!\):) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?The sense data, or the sensory qualities of the objects about which we) Tj T*
(make statements, thus are pushed steadily further back; and when we) Tj T*
(complete the process of defining all objects by explicit relations) Tj T*
(instead of by the implicit relations inherent in our sensory) Tj T*
(distinctions, those sense data disappear completely from the system. In) Tj T*
(the end the system of explicit definitions becomes both) Tj T*
(all-comprehensive and self-contained or circular; all the elements in) Tj T*
(the universe are defined by their relations to each other, and all we) Tj T*
(know about the universe becomes contained in those definitions. We) Tj T*
(should obtain a self-contained model capable of reproducing all the) Tj T*
(combinations of events which we can observe in the external world, but) Tj T*
(should have no way of ascertaining whether any particular event in the) Tj T*
(external world corresponded to a particular part of our model. Science) Tj T*
(thus tends necessarily towards an ultimate state in which all knowledge) Tj T*
(is embodied in the definitions of the object with which it is) Tj T*
ET
