(concerned; and in which all true statements about these objects) Tj T*
(therefore are analytical or tautological and could not be disproved by) Tj T*
(any experience. The observation that any object did not behave as it) Tj T*
(should could then only mean that it was not an object of the kind it) Tj T*
(was thought to be. With the disappearence of all sensory data from the) Tj T*
