(I have presented a ?logic of exceptions? that changes the argument.) Tj T*
(\(Not in this book.\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.       See our discussion on non-Euclidean geometry in the main body) Tj T*
(of the text.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4.       On p23 Barrow suggests that at small dimensions ?concepts?) Tj T*
(like velocity and position can only exist with ?limited sharpness? -) Tj T*
(which is a very strange thing to say.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5.       Barrow p22 states: ?There have occasionally been attempts to) Tj T*
(find mental consequences of Heisenberg uncertainty, but the general) Tj T*
(opinion is that the effects are too small on the scale of neurons to) Tj T*
(have any significant effect upon the human thinking process.? Well,) Tj T*
(Schrödinger gave his cat-example that quantum mechanics can extend into) Tj T*
(the macro world. \(We don?t seem to have that mechanism in our head) Tj T*
(though, but there can be equivalent ones.\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6.       We should be more critical about how physicists deal with) Tj T*
(their ?measurement problems? in general.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
