() Tj T*
(As an economic expert I advise to a parliamentary enquiry and a public) Tj T*
(debate on this issue. It are the present powers in government that must) Tj T*
(grow convinced of the need for a better balance of powers. The evidence) Tj T*
(will likely convince them, if only they study it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The following is a text that may serve as a concept for a) Tj T*
(constitutional amendment. The text assumes the common Trias Politica.) Tj T*
(It uses the term ?Parliament? for the legislative branch \(e.g. US) Tj T*
(Congress\), and ?President? for the executive branch \(e.g. the UK) Tj T*
(Cabinet\). It then adds the Economic Supreme Court. The given size,) Tj T*
(terms and other properties of the Economic Supreme Court seem best to) Tj T*
(create a balance for group decision making, openness, stability and) Tj T*
(change.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This text has essentially been posted on the internet in 1996. The) Tj T*
(major current change with respect to that text is a result of Frank) Tj T*
(Sulloway?s ?Born to rebel? \(1996\) and the subsequent reports - Van den) Tj T*
(Berg \(2004\) refers to _Nature_ - that these findings are not accurate.) Tj T*
(Sulloway argues that first-borns tend to be less open to new ideas but) Tj T*
(more likely to have responsible positions. This causes the idea that,) Tj T*
(since the court should be sensitive to new discoveries and be critical) Tj T*
(to abuse of authority, it would seem wise to have some test on) Tj T*
(open-mindedness. This needs to be investigated upon. Since this is a) Tj T*
(constitution, we should formulate a general rule, and we should leave) Tj T*
(it to the practical times and state of scientific inquiry how this is) Tj T*
(implemented, by first-bornnesss or by some other verifiable criterion.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The nation has an independent and scientific Economic Supreme Court of) Tj T*
(equal status next to Parliament, the President and the Supreme Court.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. The task of the Court is to scientifically check the economic data,) Tj T*
(assumptions, analyses and projections underlying the government?s) Tj T*
(budget and its draft statement, and then possibly veto the official) Tj T*
(adoption and publication of the budget, if the Court finds that the) Tj T*
(information used and presented, and in particular the estimates for the) Tj T*
(deficit and national debt, are not scientifically correct. The Court) Tj T*
(will publish its findings both for Parliament and for the scientific) Tj T*
(community.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Members of the Court are appointed by the Court itself, subject to a) Tj T*
(veto by a normal majority in Parliament.) Tj T*
(The Court will inform Parliament about the name and credentials of the) Tj T*
(candidate for appointment. Parliament will have 50 days to discuss and) Tj T*
(possibly veto an appointment. The appointment of the candidate becomes) Tj T*
(effective when Parliament does not veto the appointment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. The Court consists of 7 members. At least 5 members have a high) Tj T*
(likelihood of open-mindedness, by criteria generally accepted in the) Tj T*
(scientific community.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Term rules are:) Tj T*
