() Tj T*
(a\) Each member serves a term of 7 years. Each year the member with the) Tj T*
(longest term resigns, and a new member is appointed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(b\)       Terms run from May 1st till April 30st, 7 years later. If a) Tj T*
(member resigns before the end of the term, then the replacement will) Tj T*
(concern only the remainder of the term.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(c\)       Members may only serve for two terms, which terms need not be) Tj T*
(consecutive. A part term will not count if its duration is less than 4) Tj T*
(years.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(d\)       All 7 members participate in the selection of a candidate for) Tj T*
(appointment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(e\) The Court chooses its chairperson from among its members.) Tj T*
(Non-eligible are the newly appointed and the resigning member, so that) Tj T*
(only 5 members are eligible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(f\) The Court determines its modus operandi further by itself.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Parliament may, if the occasion arises, decide to dismiss an) Tj T*
(existing Court and reappoint a new one, which decision requires a) Tj T*
(majority of two-thirds. Parliament may not override a veto by the) Tj T*
(Court, by any majority. It is up to the newly installed Court to decide) Tj T*
(if a wronged veto is repealed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. The means of the Court are as follows:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(a\) The Court can appoint a staff of maximally 150 persons. Minimally) Tj T*
(50% of the staff shall have an appointment as scientist, and they shall) Tj T*
(operate under both common scientific standards and a special statute) Tj T*
(that has precedence. This special statute shall be established and) Tj T*
(published by the Court.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(b\)       The Court can instruct the President to provide information.) Tj T*
(The President may refuse information only if national security is at) Tj T*
(stake. Information that the President regards as confidential will be) Tj T*
(treated as confidential by the Court and its staff too, unless the same) Tj T*
(information can be received via independent other channels too.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(c\)       When State governments within the Federation install their own) Tj T*
(Economic Courts, then possible disputes shall be settled by the) Tj T*
(Economic Supreme Court.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(d\)       The Court can install a council of economists and other) Tj T*
(specialists from the academia. The Court can install chambers of) Tj T*
(special competence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(e\) The Court shall have a budget that compares favourably to the) Tj T*
(average budget of scientific research institutes of the same size.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
