(A parallel argument on the Central Bank) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The analysis about the Economic Supreme Court and the ?natural) Tj T*
(monopoly? argument about economic policy advice, actually finds a) Tj T*
(parallel with respect to the Central Bank. Reading Galbraith \(1998\)) Tj T*
(made me aware of this situation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Let us regard the situation that market forces determine the rate of) Tj T*
(interest to a large extent, but that the Bank is not without some power) Tj T*
(and will use its influence on rates to control inflation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Theory dependence: The Bank decides on its policy while using an) Tj T*
(economic model that contains a mechanism for the determination of the) Tj T*
(rate of interest - for example the rate of interest will contain) Tj T*
(anticipated inflation. Hence policy is directly dependent upon the) Tj T*
(state of economic theory.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Self-reference \(reflexiveness\): Since interest rates are sensitive to) Tj T*
(Bank policy, Bank policy would be part of the model. Popular thought) Tj T*
(has it that a good Bank would target at zero inflation, but Bank policy) Tj T*
(generally would be different. For example, a true zero target would) Tj T*
(require that a period with inflation is followed by deflation, and) Tj T*
(Banks generally don?t do that. Also, the true price level should) Tj T*
(include inventories and capital stocks, but inflation generally is) Tj T*
(measured as the CPI, which is something totally different. These) Tj T*
(details, and Bank policies on them, should be put into the model \(with) Tj T*
(error terms to allow for possible discretion\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Conflictive self-reference: Clearly, one can conceive the situation) Tj T*
(that the Bank announces a policy while the true scientific forecast) Tj T*
(shows that the policy is untenable and will be repealed later. Hence) Tj T*
(there is an internal source of conflict - the worst kind, not a) Tj T*
(dysfunctional person, but a logical knot.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· General conflict of interests: The Central Bank may not only have the) Tj T*
(objective to control inflation but also other objectives, like for) Tj T*
(example supporting and supervising the financial system. For example,) Tj T*
(the US Fed is not purely a governmental body, but it is rooted in the) Tj T*
(financial system and it is influenced by private interests therein. See) Tj T*
(Galbraith \(1998:221-231\) for a discussion on the conflict of interests) Tj T*
(- for example on the ?credit crunch? - and read also Krugman on the) Tj T*
(Savings & Loans debacle.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Hence, along the ?TP & ESC? line of argumentation, we can clearly see a) Tj T*
(need for reform in existing Central Banking, and the direction that it) Tj T*
(would need to take. Interestingly, where economic policy of the state) Tj T*
(would have to be co-ordinated with the policy of the Central Bank \(that) Tj T*
(should best remain independent\), there arise questions of structure and) Tj T*
(priority. My suggestion is to first create the Economic Supreme Court,) Tj T*
(and have it advise on how to position the Bank or its separate) Tj T*
(functions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
