(About the US Council of Economic Advisers) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This appendix consists of two large quotes from the White House) Tj T*
(internet site in January 2000, with my comments added.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(From the ?Employment Act of 1946?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?There is hereby created in the Executive Office of the President a) Tj T*
(Council of Economic Advisers \(hereinafter called the ?Council?\). The) Tj T*
(Council shall be composed of three members who shall be appointed by) Tj T*
(the President, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate, and) Tj T*
(each of whom shall be a person who, as a result of his training,) Tj T*
(experience, and attainments, is exceptionally qualified to analyze and) Tj T*
(interpret economic developments, to appraise programs and activities of) Tj T*
(the Government in the light of the policy declared in section 2, and to) Tj T*
(formulate and recommend national economic policy to promote employment,) Tj T*
(production, and purchasing power under free competitive enterprise.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It shall be the duty and function of the Council--) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1.       to assist and advise the President in the preparation of the) Tj T*
(Economic Report;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2.       to gather timely and authoritative information concerning) Tj T*
(economic developments and economic trends, both current and) Tj T*
(prospective, to analyze and interpret such information in the light of) Tj T*
(the policy declared in section 2 for the purpose of determining whether) Tj T*
(such developments and trends are interfering, or are likely to) Tj T*
(interfere, with the achievement of such policy, and to compile and) Tj T*
(submit to the President studies relating to such developments and) Tj T*
(trends;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3.       to appraise the various programs and activities of the Federal) Tj T*
(Government in the light of the policy declared in section 2 for the) Tj T*
(purpose of determining the extent to which such programs and activities) Tj T*
(are contributing, and the extent to which they are not contributing, to) Tj T*
(the achievement of such policy, and to make recommendations to the) Tj T*
(President with respect thereto;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4.       to develop and recommend to the President national economic) Tj T*
(policies to foster and promote free competitive enterprise, to avoid) Tj T*
(economic fluctuations or to diminish the effects thereof, and to) Tj T*
(maintain employment, production, and purchasing power;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5.       to make and furnish such studies, reports thereon, and) Tj T*
(recommendations with respect to matters of Federal economic policy and) Tj T*
(legislation as the President may request. ?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Martin Feldstein on the US Council of Economic Advisers) Tj T*
() Tj T*
