(Martin Feldstein.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Structure of the Council of Economic Advisers) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Although the term ?Council? conjures up the image of a large committee,) Tj T*
(the CEA actually consists only of a chairman and two members. The) Tj T*
(chairman is legally responsible for establishing the positions taken by) Tj T*
(the Council. The other two members direct research activities of the) Tj T*
(Council in particular fields, represent the Council at meetings with) Tj T*
(other agencies, and generally work with the chairman to formulate) Tj T*
(economic advice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In addition to the chairman and two other members, the CEA has a) Tj T*
(professional staff that is both small and unusual. A group of about ten) Tj T*
(economists, generally professors on one- or two-year leaves from their) Tj T*
(universities, act as the senior staff economists. They in turn are) Tj T*
(assisted by an additional ten junior staff economists, typically) Tj T*
(advanced graduate students who also spend only a year or two at the) Tj T*
(CEA. Four permanent economic statisticians assist the economists in the) Tj T*
(interpretation and identification of economic data.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The academic nature of the staff and of most CEA members distinguishes) Tj T*
(the CEA from other government agencies. It generally assures a higher) Tj T*
(level of technical economic sophistication and of familiarity with) Tj T*
(current developments in economic thinking. Members and staff also use) Tj T*
(their strong links in the academic community to obtain advice on) Tj T*
(technical issues throughout their time in Washington.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is of course a price to be paid for this reliance on academic) Tj T*
(economists, especially at the staff level. They often come to the CEA) Tj T*
(without the institutional knowledge of some of the issues with which) Tj T*
(they will deal and without any experience in the bureaucratic process) Tj T*
(of decision-making. My experience however was that most of the senior) Tj T*
(staff economists learned quite quickly to be effective participants,) Tj T*
(and made an important contribution to the policy debates because of) Tj T*
(their ability to apply economic analysis to the issues being discussed,) Tj T*
(and to develop new economic proposals that had not occurred to) Tj T*
(non-economist participants from the agencies.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(How Advice Is Given) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The CEA chairman gives advice directly to the President and to the) Tj T*
(senior members of the administration. There is also a broader role of) Tj T*
(trying to shape public understanding of the economic issues. The CEA) Tj T*
(members and staff participate directly in the inter-agency process, in) Tj T*
(which policy options are evaluated and recommendations developed for) Tj T*
(presidential decisions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The specific organization of advice-giving undoubtedly differs from) Tj T*
(administration to administration, reflecting the overall form of) Tj T*
(economic policy making and the particular style and interest of the) Tj T*
(president. I can only describe my own experience.) Tj T*
ET
