() Tj T*
(In the Reagan administration, the cabinet as a whole rarely met.) Tj T*
(Instead, economic policy issues were discussed through a series of) Tj T*
(cabinet councils with more specialized responsibilities. These included) Tj T*
(a cabinet council on commerce and trade that was chaired by the) Tj T*
(Secretary of Commerce, a cabinet council that dealt with labour and) Tj T*
(social insurance issues, a cabinet council that dealt with regulatory) Tj T*
(and legal issues, and a general cabinet council on economic affairs) Tj T*
(that was chaired by the Secretary of the Treasury. Each of the) Tj T*
(interested departments was represented at the council by the secretary) Tj T*
(of that department. Occasionally the deputy secretary or) Tj T*
(under-secretary substituted for the secretary at those meetings. I) Tj T*
(generally represented the CEA, although occasionally one of the members) Tj T*
(took my place at the table. Vice President Bush usually attended these) Tj T*
(meetings.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The councils generally met without the president. Roughly twice a month) Tj T*
(the president participated in council meetings when there was a) Tj T*
(specific issue that required a presidential decision or, occasionally,) Tj T*
(a broad area that seemed appropriate for general cabinet-level) Tj T*
(discussion with the president.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Any major proposal for legislative action, whether originated by a) Tj T*
(department or from Congress, would be assigned to an appropriate) Tj T*
(cabinet council for consideration to develop an official administration) Tj T*
(position. Initial meetings would be held at a staff level, with the CEA) Tj T*
(represented by the senior staff economist with the relevant expertise.) Tj T*
(Often discussion at this level would be sufficient to dispose of the) Tj T*
(idea, usually with the conclusion that the proposal was well-meaning) Tj T*
(but misguided and would not accomplish its stated purpose or would do) Tj T*
(so only at an unacceptable economic cost. This would quietly bury an) Tj T*
(internal departmental proposal or lead to a formal administration) Tj T*
(position to oppose a Congressional initiative.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When there was disagreement about the proposal that could not be) Tj T*
(resolved unanimously at the level of this working group, a higher-level) Tj T*
(meeting would be held. Each interested department would be represented) Tj T*
(at a sub-cabinet level, generally by an assistant secretary. The CEA) Tj T*
(would be represented by a member or senior staff economist, since with) Tj T*
(only two members it was often true that the CEA only had the expertise) Tj T*
(at the senior staff level and preferred to send a real expert rather) Tj T*
(than, as in the other departments, to send a more senior official who) Tj T*
(was ?briefed? but who did not really understand the issues himself.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Once again, if this group could not reach a consensus the issue would) Tj T*
(be passed up to the full cabinet council, where the departments were) Tj T*
(represented at the top level and the CEA by the chairman. If this group) Tj T*
(reached an agreed recommendation, its conclusion would be sent to the) Tj T*
(President. When there was disagreement, a summary of the different) Tj T*
(positions would be prepared by the staff of the council for submission) Tj T*
(to the president for his decision. These decision memos were carefully) Tj T*
(prepared so that each side could object to any spurious arguments put) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
