(the advice being given by that department?s own economist. In other) Tj T*
(cases, it fills a gap where the department does not have an economist) Tj T*
(or where the CEA can bring better analysis to a particular problem. As) Tj T*
(chairman I also met on an individual basis with the department heads to) Tj T*
(discuss policy issues relevant to their department or more general) Tj T*
(issues like the budget situation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A weekly breakfast meeting with the Treasury Secretary and the OMB) Tj T*
(Director -- the so-called Troika or T-t group -- provided an important) Tj T*
(opportunity to discuss economic issues with complete candour and) Tj T*
(without fear of leaks to the press. This small group was occasionally) Tj T*
(joined by Secretary of State George Shultz and on some rare occasions) Tj T*
(by Federal Reserve Chairman Paul Volcker.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These breakfast meetings were just about the only time during my time) Tj T*
(at the CEA when the Fed Chairman participated in a discussion inside) Tj T*
(the administration. He met privately of course with the Secretary of) Tj T*
(the Treasury and with various financial regulators. I had breakfast) Tj T*
(with him every other week and on those occasions we discussed the state) Tj T*
(of the economy, the direction of monetary policy, banking regulation,) Tj T*
(and such issues as the developing country debt problem, in which the) Tj T*
(Fed worked closely with the administration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As the senior economist in the administration, the CEA chairman is) Tj T*
(frequently called upon to discuss economic policy issues in public.) Tj T*
(These include testimony to congressional committees, speeches to a wide) Tj T*
(array of audiences, occasional television interviews and frequent) Tj T*
(discussions with the press. I always regarded these as opportunities to) Tj T*
(teach economics. An important challenge was to explain why the dollar) Tj T*
(had soared and how that, rather than protectionist policies abroad, was) Tj T*
(responsible for our trade deficit. Until the recovery was firmly) Tj T*
(established, I would explain why an expansionary fiscal policy was) Tj T*
(unnecessary and later I spent endless hours explaining how to assess) Tj T*
(the structural budget deficit and why reducing it was important.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Council of Economic Advisers produces an annual report which) Tj T*
(discusses broad issues of economic policy for a general audience. This) Tj T*
(report is widely read by the economic press, by Congressional staff and) Tj T*
(by academic economists and students.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(How the CEA Advises Presidents) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_?I think our unique system of placing a professional economist in the) Tj T*
(White House to report directly to the president works well. I hope that) Tj T*
(future presidents continue to use this policy.?_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The principle of comparative advantage suggests that I, as a former) Tj T*
(chairman of the Council of Economic Advisers, convey my knowledge of) Tj T*
(this unique and little understood agency. I emphasize the word ?unique?) Tj T*
(because I believe the CEA is really quite different from advisory) Tj T*
(institutions in other countries.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
