stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(During my time as chairman \(1982 through 1984\), I had the opportunity) Tj T*
(to talk with the senior economic officials in many countries. I never) Tj T*
(found one that institutionalized our combination of characteristics: a) Tj T*
(professional economist who has direct access to the head of the) Tj T*
(government and who participates as an equal in all cabinet-level) Tj T*
(discussions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In other countries, the top economic official is either an economics) Tj T*
(minister \(i.e., a politician selected from the Parliament who may or) Tj T*
(may not be a professional economist\) or a professional economist who) Tj T*
(reports to the minister of finance or some other cabinet minister.) Tj T*
(There are also some special situations in which individual economists) Tj T*
(are influential advisers to the heads of government, but these are) Tj T*
(personal arrangements that have not been institutionalized in the way) Tj T*
(that the CEA has been.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One reason why the American system for giving economic advice differs) Tj T*
(from those abroad is that, in our presidential system, it is the) Tj T*
(president rather than the minister of finance or budget minister who) Tj T*
(has ultimate responsibility for all economic matters. In other) Tj T*
(countries, the prime minister or president is less involved with) Tj T*
(economic issues and the responsible cabinet member has a political) Tj T*
(standing and legitimacy in his own right. In the United States, the) Tj T*
(cabinet is in the last analysis an advisory and management body while) Tj T*
(all true decision-making authority of the executive branch is vested in) Tj T*
(the president.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The role of the CEA and its chairman undoubtedly differs over time) Tj T*
(depending on both the chairman and the president. The differences can) Tj T*
(be quite profound even within the same set of legal rules. For example,) Tj T*
(during the Nixon administration there was a period when George Shultz) Tj T*
(served simultaneously as budget director and as counselor to the) Tj T*
(president with responsibility for overall coordination of economic) Tj T*
(advice. But I have not researched the history of the CEA and will) Tj T*
(therefore focus my comments on the period of 1982-1984 that I know from) Tj T*
(firsthand experience.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I began by saying that the council is ?little understood? because I) Tj T*
(have frequently discovered that people are quite surprised when they) Tj T*
(learn how small the council is and how it actually operates. The term) Tj T*
(?council? seems to conjure up the image of a dozen or more people) Tj T*
(sitting around a conference table voting on recommendations of economic) Tj T*
(policy. In fact, the CEA has only a chairman and two additional) Tj T*
(members.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Since the days of the Arthur Burns? chairmanship in the Eisenhower) Tj T*
(administration, there has been an official executive order vesting all) Tj T*
(of the executive authority for the council in the chairman. In) Tj T*
(practice, that means that the three members have informal discussions) Tj T*
(but do not take votes. It also means that when a formal recommendation) Tj T*
(from several agencies is sent to the president, the position taken by) Tj T*
(the CEA reflects the judgment of the chairman just as the position of) Tj T*
ET
endstream
