(Leadership Council, A New $21 Billion Plan to Expand the Earned Income) Tj T*
(Tax Credit -- A Key Part of His ?New Opportunity Agenda.? The) Tj T*
(President?s proposal would expand the Earned Income Tax Credit \(EITC\)) Tj T*
(to provide tax relief for 6.4 million hard-pressed working families.) Tj T*
(The expansion will cost about $21 billion over 10 years.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Building on the Successes of the 1993 EITC Expansion. In 1993, the) Tj T*
(President signed into law the largest EITC expansion ever to provide a) Tj T*
(tax cut for 15 million working families while rewarding work and) Tj T*
(family. Today, the success of the EITC in reducing poverty and) Tj T*
(encouraging work is clear:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· 4.3 Million People Directly Lifted Out of Poverty by the EITC in 1998) Tj T*
(-- more than double the number lifted out of poverty in 1993.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· 2.3 Million Children Directly Lifted Out of Poverty by the EITC in) Tj T*
(1998. This includes 600,000 African-American children and 600,000) Tj T*
(Hispanic children..) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Largest Drop in Poverty and Child Poverty in Over Three Decades. The) Tj T*
(poverty rate has fallen from 15.1 percent in 1993 to 12.7 percent in) Tj T*
(1998 -- the lowest since 1979. At the same time, the child poverty rate) Tj T*
(fell from 22.7 percent to 18.9 percent -- the lowest child poverty rate) Tj T*
(since 1980.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· More Single Mom?s Are Working Than Ever Before. The percentage of) Tj T*
(single mothers who work and receive no welfare has risen from 60.9) Tj T*
(percent in 1992 to 75.0 percent in 1998.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The President?s Proposal Increases the Reward to Work and Family in) Tj T*
(Four Ways:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Expand the Maximum Credit for Working Families with Three or More) Tj T*
(Children By $500. This would provide a tax break for 2.1 million low-) Tj T*
(and moderate-income working families. This expansion is targeted at the) Tj T*
(highest concentration of child poverty: in 1998 the poverty rate for) Tj T*
(children in families with three or more related children was 28.5) Tj T*
(percent -- more than twice the 11.9 percent poverty rate for children) Tj T*
(in families with one or two related children.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Expand the Credit for Married, Two-Earner Couples. This would benefit) Tj T*
(over 1.3 million married filers. For married, two-earner couples, this) Tj T*
(provision by itself would provide an average tax break of $250.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Increase the Reward to Work While Expanding the Credit for Families) Tj T*
(with Two or More Children. This would provide an additional tax break,) Tj T*
(and an additional incentive to work, for families with two or more) Tj T*
(children by lowering the phase-out rate to give more rewards to) Tj T*
(families struggling to work their way into the middle class.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(· Encouraging Savings Through Simplification. Currently, when a working) Tj T*
(family contributes to a 401\(k\) they may see their EITC reduced. This) Tj T*
ET
