(business process that comes closest to the problem of the Productivity) Tj T*
(Slowdown. Namely, when inventories are reduced, then this normally) Tj T*
(means that part of demand is serviced from inventories, and this means) Tj T*
(lower production. Estimating stylized relationships for the US, we find) Tj T*
(that inventories in 1997 are 25% lower than they would have been) Tj T*
(otherwise, and the level of production is 0.56% lower at an annual) Tj T*
