() Tj T*
(A note on the New Economy \(2000\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(The following note was written in 2000 and it still stands in 2004.\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The US economy has shown steady growth from 1992 till 2000, and people) Tj T*
(have been talking about a New Economy.  The stock exchange has) Tj T*
(exploded, the Productivity Slowdown seems to be over, unemployment has) Tj T*
(been dropping below the CWIRU \(NAIRU\) while prices have remained) Tj T*
(stable, an Asian Crisis that might have turned into a big depression) Tj T*
(did not do that: and economists have been looking all over to find) Tj T*
(causes. The New Economy answer would be that the Volcker - Reagan years) Tj T*
(have created a stable environment, and that technology now is causing) Tj T*
(all kinds of revolutions. Computers, the internet, biology, a better) Tj T*
(understanding of economics and capital markets, you name what, the) Tj T*
(interaction of all these: they all cause a wholly different world. And) Tj T*
(billionaires to prove it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(My view on this issue is sensibly guarded.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Yes, the internet indeed has interesting properties, vide Shapiro &) Tj T*
(Varian \(1999\). I have been using computers intensively since 1972, have) Tj T*
(my own software on the internet - see Colignatus \(1999\). Yes, on) Tj T*
(biology and other technologies the possibilities are huge, and man can) Tj T*
(be a creative animal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(No, it all is plain old economics. Shapiro & Varian \(1999\) make that) Tj T*
(clear too. Also: \(a\) It should be obvious by now that my own analysis) Tj T*
(on unemployment and inflation already provides much of the answers.) Tj T*
(Many causes why the CWIRU dropped can be identified - e.g. the EITC) Tj T*
(increase \(labour cost reduction\) in 1993, and the abolishing of) Tj T*
(?welfare as we know it?. Society has started to accept a lower) Tj T*
(subsistence level - which is a dubious origin of growth for the rich.) Tj T*
(\(b\) Lower taxes for the rich gives them more money e.g. to invest in) Tj T*
(the stock market. \(c\) Americans have been borrowing. \(d\) The fact that) Tj T*
(1970-1992 was a low period in post-War US history does not mean that) Tj T*
(the current ?high? is so high. I think that the basic foundation was) Tj T*
(given by FDR, and hence the creative human energy was provided with a) Tj T*
(stable environment to prosper. The 1970-1992 period fouled up the FDR) Tj T*
(heritage. Getting back to that heritage is important - but not) Tj T*
(something ?new?. \(e\) Of course there still are many people in poverty,) Tj T*
