(\(8\)    The following comments can be included at this very spot:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(a\)    Much of current policy focus is on the EU Lissabon Strategy and) Tj T*
(issues like pensions. This book does not explicitly discuss these but) Tj T*
(it would be a mistake to conclude that this book would not be relevant) Tj T*
(for those topics. The point is that this book already had that long) Tj T*
(term approach to start with. Lissabon and pensions are new kids on the) Tj T*
(block and one should rather study this book before proceeding with new) Tj T*
(policy making.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(b\)    Advised reading is Skidelsky \(2000\), the third part of his) Tj T*
(biography of Keynes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(c\)    Lomborg \(2001\), ?The skeptical environmentalist. Measuring the) Tj T*
(real state of the world?, gives an impressive review of the problems in) Tj T*
(this subject. As an economist and non-ecologist it is difficult for me) Tj T*
(to say anything about his comments on the state of the ecology. Three) Tj T*
(statements in the realm of political economy are:) Tj T*
(\(b1\) Lomborg does not yet take account of the argument by Hueting) Tj T*
(\(1980\) and Van Ierland et al. \(2001\). Statistical measurement of) Tj T*
(national income derives from the economic theory of social welfare. To) Tj T*
(approximate the social welfare function we use the income hyperplane) Tj T*
(that is tangent to it. Market prices for the environment will not) Tj T*
(suffice since there are market failures.) Tj T*
(\(b2\) In his discussion on the ?double dividend? Lomborg relies on) Tj T*
(economic papers that do not take into account both the analysis by) Tj T*
(Hueting and the analysis provided in this book on the Trias Politica,) Tj T*
(unemployment, the tax void and dynamic marginal rates.) Tj T*
(\(b3\) The case for an Economic Supreme Court appears enhanced. Human) Tj T*
(flourishing requires proper environmental protection, and monitoring of) Tj T*
(the information about the environment then requires proper safeguards.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(d\)    Shiller \(2003\), ?The new financial order. Risk in the 21st) Tj T*
(century?, discusses how the market with proper government regulation) Tj T*
(can give rise to new risk instruments. Part of what I try to do with) Tj T*
(the constitutional amendment for an Economic Supreme Court, he tries to) Tj T*
(do with ?macro-markets?, i.e. financial instruments based upon macro) Tj T*
(variables: namely, getting better information. My impression is that) Tj T*
(both approaches have merits of their own, and that it helps to) Tj T*
(disentangle what the instruments are intended for precisely. Similarly,) Tj T*
(the analysis in this book on unemployment cannot be replaced by an) Tj T*
(insurance on the distribution of income. Yet, when these more basic) Tj T*
(reforms on the Economic Supreme Court and unemployment have been) Tj T*
(implemented, Shiller is right that welfare can be improved by novel) Tj T*
(risk instruments.) Tj T*
