(\(j\)      There are some Dutch books that deserve an English) Tj T*
(translation. Here I only translate the titles. Klever \(1990\), ?Pure) Tj T*
(economic science?, takes his position in Spinoza and argues that) Tj T*
(economic science should be developed from first principles in a) Tj T*
(deductive fashion. This strikes me as quite similar to the ?definition) Tj T*
(& reality methodology?. Mathematical economics already had the) Tj T*
(deductive approach, and econometrics assumed that only statistical) Tj T*
(approximation was feasible, but we can do better if we can find) Tj T*
(definitions that fit stylized facts. Klever also recovered Franciscus) Tj T*
(van den Enden \(1665, 1992\), ?Free political theses?. That author was a) Tj T*
(teacher of Spinoza and his book argues that democracy is the only form) Tj T*
(of government that can safeguard stability and general welfare. Klever) Tj T*
(\(1981\), ?Dialectic thinking?, must be mentioned for a better) Tj T*
(understanding of the deductive method. His discussion of Poincaré and) Tj T*
(his pupils, for example, clarifies the creative element in mathematics.) Tj T*
(Guépin \(1985\) ?Civilization? and Guépin \(1994\) ?The difference in) Tj T*
(opinion? defend classical rhetorics as the essence of civilized) Tj T*
(mentality. These books provide a wealth of information and are a useful) Tj T*
(antidote to expecting too much from deduction only. He highlights the) Tj T*
(tension between rhetorics and deduction by criticizing Socrates that it) Tj T*
(is rather easy to impress people by goading them into inconsistencies) Tj T*
(when they have not first defined their terms properly. \(Rhetorics) Tj T*
(cannot make fun of rule based inference if the only goal of rhetorics) Tj T*
(is to get better inference.\) Guépin also highlights that deduction) Tj T*
(thrives with dichotomy but hesitates with the _sorites_, i.e. the) Tj T*
(problem of accumulating grains of sand until the mountain moves.) Tj T*
