(The analysis shows mathematically that democratic goals indeed can be) Tj T*
(blocked by special interests or neglect, for example within the) Tj T*
(bureaucracy. A policy conclusion is to improve informational \(planning\)) Tj T*
(procedures.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The discussion of taxes, unemployment and inflation is basically just a) Tj T*
(minor point of the book. The major point of the book concerns the) Tj T*
(co-ordination problem. Western democracies apparently allow long) Tj T*
(periods like the Great Depression or the Great Stagflation that are) Tj T*
(detrimental to the economic well-being and security of large sections) Tj T*
(of their populations. Ideas of economists that point the way to) Tj T*
(recovery are only slowly accepted. Key examples are the ideas of) Tj T*
(Tinbergen and Keynes: for them it took World War II before they got) Tj T*
(listened to. Eventually, the political powers of that time accepted) Tj T*
(that they had to redesign the structure of economic policy making, and) Tj T*
(they gave more room to the scientists, but did not dare to give up) Tj T*
(their ultimate power to meddle with the information. Currently, the) Tj T*
(world faces the challenge of the growth of the world population from 6) Tj T*
(billion people around 2000 to likely around 8 billion people around) Tj T*
(2025. To manage this process, mankind would benefit from a structure of) Tj T*
(economic decision making that is both democratic and that respects the) Tj T*
(citizen?s right to know.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
