([12] An illustrative example of the statics vs. dynamics issue, and of) Tj T*
(the problems that economists continue to have in making this) Tj T*
(distinction, is page 125 of Gregory Mankiw?s 1998 ?Principles of) Tj T*
(economics? edition. Concerning the payroll tax and the distribution of) Tj T*
(its burden over firms and workers, and using a diagram of elastic) Tj T*
(demand and supply, he states: ?This division of the tax burden between) Tj T*
(workers and firms does not depend on whether the government levies the) Tj T*
(tax on workers, levies the tax on firms, or divides the tax equally) Tj T*
(between the two groups.? Referring to a US Congress effort to allocate) Tj T*
(the burden he concludes: ?This example shows that the most basic lesson) Tj T*
(of tax incidence is often overlooked in public debate.? Well, this) Tj T*
(conclusion is only valid for the static analysis, but in dynamics, take) Tj T*
(home pay is directly affected by regulations, while wage contracts are) Tj T*
(adjusted by quite different bargaining processes. The US Congress may) Tj T*
(well have taken a right decision for the medium run.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([13] I will take the position that definitions \(and thus tautologies\)) Tj T*
(can be very important too. I tend to think that Samuelson in fact would) Tj T*
(not disagree if the point would be formulated as such. Indeed,) Tj T*
(Samuelson has remained more of a theorist himself, and is less known) Tj T*
(for work on collecting data and estimation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([14] Western economies suffer since the early 1970s from mass) Tj T*
(unemployment and the threat of inflation. This bad mix of bad) Tj T*
(ingredients is called ?stagflation? for short. ?Stagflation? in fact is) Tj T*
(a concatenation of ?stagnation? and ?inflation?. The word was coined) Tj T*
(around 1970 when national income growth stagnated and brought along) Tj T*
(unemployment. Since then growth has somewhat recovered, and stagflation) Tj T*
(has been redefined and now is properly understood as a bad ?trade-off?) Tj T*
(of both inflation and unemployment. See below.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([15] Note that Kennedy \(1999\) in his first six pages prominently refers) Tj T*
(to Keynes \(1919\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([16] UN-WIDER Press Release ?40 International Experts and Scholars Meet) Tj T*
(in Helsinki to Discuss the Wave of New Emergencies, 6 - 8 October 1996,) Tj T*
(at Hotel Marski?.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([17] Interview with Kruiderink, ?Progress ? No, it is a black hole.?) Tj T*
(Volkskrant Oct. 16 1999) Tj T*
() Tj T*
