(1993.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([119] If ?animal spirits? is not properly explained, it generates) Tj T*
(confusion. As this confusion exists, perhaps I need to provide this) Tj T*
(explanation here as well: Medieval philosophy distinguished between) Tj T*
(dead matter, plants and objects with a spirit - and the Latin word for) Tj T*
(spirit/mind is ?animus?. So Keynes?s reference is not to wild beasts,) Tj T*
(though Mankiw suggests such with his mention of ?irrationality? and) Tj T*
(?arbitrary changes in attitude?. As I understand it, Keynes entertains) Tj T*
(the consideration that beings with a mind by definition develop) Tj T*
(conceptions about reality, and act and take decisions in a state of) Tj T*
(uncertainty.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([120] Krugman though allows for a temporary adverse development in) Tj T*
(technology. This chapter was basically written as the paper Colignatus) Tj T*
(\(1997a\), and since then Krugman has seen more scope for the technology) Tj T*
(argument.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([121] I can understand your misgivings about having to read five books) Tj T*
(before allowed to continue. Personally, I already knew most of what) Tj T*
(Krugman is writing about, and this may also be the case for you. But it) Tj T*
(was a useful refresher, lots of fun reading, and when everybody reads) Tj T*
(them then there is some common ground.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([122] That is, most economists don?t know yet, but I do, and thus ?the) Tj T*
(economics profession? knows it. In the same way, if a murderer knows) Tj T*
(that someone in the room knows that he is the villain, he is tempted to) Tj T*
(kill all in the room. This someone is going to tell !) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([123] It is good to see that James Galbraith \(1998\) takes up this issue) Tj T*
(too. See below.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([124] Note that the reason why I am quite certain about my own approach) Tj T*
(is that I have given a mathematical theorem and proof based upon) Tj T*
(readily acceptable premisses. I also use a reduced form, but, deduction) Tj T*
(beats econometric testing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([125] In 1997 I also wrote ?\(?bargaining?\) has more to do with the) Tj T*
(level of wages than the \(inflationary\) rate of change.? I have to) Tj T*
(retract that statement. I temporarily forgot my very own analysis on) Tj T*
(the Phillipscurve ! Yes, I must have been irritated.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([126] And indeed, it must be feared that mainstream economists will not) Tj T*
(be interested much in inequality, so that they will also miss out on) Tj T*
ET
