(ECONOMICS ? POLITICS ? LAW) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This book explains why the world economy enjoyed a golden period in the) Tj T*
(years 1950-1970 and what went wrong since then. Europe in 2005 has a) Tj T*
(\(hidden\) unemployment of 10% and relies on an extensive benefit system) Tj T*
(to prevent poverty. The US has less unemployment but at the price of) Tj T*
(more poverty ? making Europe reluctant to adopt that model. The world) Tj T*
(as a whole is a political and economic mess with much and extreme human) Tj T*
(suffering. Policymakers explain developments by causes such as) Tj T*
(globalisation, technology and welfare state sclerosis. Those) Tj T*
(explanations are not convincing however since trade and technology are) Tj T*
(sources for welfare, while the only answer to poverty is a well managed) Tj T*
(welfare state. This book provides an explanation based upon a new) Tj T*
(approach.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When democracies fail to care for their citizens, the cause must be) Tj T*
(looked for in the political system. The cause for the present failure) Tj T*
(can be found in the Trias Politica structure of national decision) Tj T*
(making ? the separation of powers of the Executive, Legislative and) Tj T*
(Judiciary branches of government. This structure gives too much room) Tj T*
(for political elites and bureaucrats to neglect the basic rights of the) Tj T*
(population at large. This approach provides an extension and follow-up) Tj T*
(to the "General Theory" of John Maynard Keynes. Inclusion of economic) Tj T*
(decision making into the analysis gives a truly General Theory of) Tj T*
(Political Economy. The theory shows that a constitutional amendment for) Tj T*
