(an Economic Supreme Court is required ? for logical reasons, for the) Tj T*
(experience of the whole 20th century, and for an actual improvement of) Tj T*
(real democracy which is so much needed for the 21st century.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An example of the policy failure is the curious  phenomenon of the Tax) Tj T*
(Void. The tax void is the income range between the net and gross) Tj T*
(minimum wage. Since people may not work below the gross minimum, those) Tj T*
(affected don?t earn income and don?t pay taxes. The taxman intends to) Tj T*
(collect taxes in that range, but since there are no earnings there, he) Tj T*
(doesn?t collect anything. The tax code only drives up the gross minimum) Tj T*
(wage, causing unemployment and the associated benefit burden.) Tj T*
(Abolishing that tax code would, since there are no revenues, not cost) Tj T*
(anything either ? and create jobs. During 1950-1970 net minimum wage) Tj T*
(workers were hardly taxed and such taxes were gradually introduced.) Tj T*
(Policy makers have been oblivious to this issue and have actually been) Tj T*
(neglecting sound economic advice on it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
